# Phase 5 transcript (DIFF-WRAPb): a write of a new file of twenty lines,
# so the line numbers take two columns, whose tabs land where fx's row
# walker has already run a row on -- a tab on the walker's second row
# (`\t`, 108 or 110 characters, `\t`), a tab after a row the walker filled
# to the last column, a tab on a reflowed row under the gutter, two tabs at
# the margin, a tab after a wide character in the last column and one
# before a wide character, a U+FE0F or a U+0301 after a tab, one that
# moves nothing and one that does (DIFF-WRAPc) -- and a two-digit line
# reflowed. Ctrl-O over the change:
# fx reflows each line (`reflowDiffRow`, transcript_blocks.zig:720-768
# @481104fd), then its walker places each tab from the column of the row
# it is on (full_transcript_screen.zig:4004-4031@481104fd).
gateway p5-transcript-diffwrap2-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
keep
wait 4
type write the file
wait 1
key Enter
wait 5
snap edited
key C-o
wait 2
snap full
key C-o
wait 1
snap closed
gwlog
